{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Speak… and you shall say….</b> The verse doubled, saying <b>דַּבֵּר and אָמַרְתָּ</b>, and also changed its language. Perhaps it intends two types of nazir, one more praiseworthy than the other — namely, the naziritehood of that which they said in Nedarim (Nedarim 9b), that which Shimon haTzaddik said: 'All my days I did not eat…' but once… the offering that I shave to the heavens…,' about you the verse said (Numbers 6:5) ״נָזִיר לְהַזִּיר לַה׳״ — see there. Therefore it says <b>דַּבֵּר</b> corresponding to the other naziritehood, and <b>אָמַרְתָּ</b> corresponding to the superior naziritehood. And for this reason it doubled, saying <b>נָזִיר לְהַזִּיר לַה׳</b>, and did not say merely לְהַזִּיר לַה׳: it intended to speak of two types of naziritehood — <b>נָזִיר</b> corresponding to all naziritehood that one undertakes for oneself, and the phrase <b>לְהַזִּיר לַה׳</b> corresponding to naziritehood that is from its very outset for HaShem, like the deed of that man who took naziritehood upon himself when he saw his reflection."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:06:18.981979947Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}